//! Table designer (FR-M1): create or alter a table visually — columns,
//! primary key, unique keys, indexes, foreign keys, checks, triggers,
//! options and comment — with a live DDL preview generated by the
//! connection's dialect: `create_table` for a new table, `alter_table` with
//! the tracked column renames for an existing one. Executing asks for
//! confirmation, runs on the connection's session (in one transaction where
//! the database has transactional DDL) and refreshes the metadata.
//!
//! The designer keeps its own model: columns have stable ids, so keys,
//! indexes and foreign keys follow renames and moves; objects the user did
//! not touch are given back exactly as read, so the ALTER script only
//! contains real changes.

